    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "So you're saying that even if a country has a strong legal system or democratic institutions, the ethnic divisions might just override them? If I'm looking at a specific country with a 60/40 split between two main groups, is it safe to assume that one group will always eventually try to dominate the other through conflict, just because of their cultural makeup?",
