      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a very real possibility that ethnic divisions can undermine even the strongest legal frameworks. When groups feel their cultural identity or perceived historical rights are threatened, the \"rule of law\" often becomes secondary to tribal loyalty. With a 60/40 split, the dominant group will naturally seek to consolidate power, and the minority group will feel compelled to resist, leading to tension. Assuming conflict is always inevitable is too strong, but assuming stability without accounting for that inherent tension is dangerously naive.",
